# Environment for `website (free AI)` in .claude/launch.json.
#
# The local SQLite database, with AI generation running on Groq's free tier
# instead of Anthropic. Nothing here is billed, and nothing touches the
# production database.
#
# YOU ADD ONE THING: a Groq key, in baakhapaa-backend/.env (never here):
#     GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...
# Free, no card: https://console.groq.com/keys
# Without it the backend refuses to start and says so, which is deliberate —
# a provider that silently fell back to canned output would look like a bug in
# the scene generator.
#
# WHY GROQ, AND WHY THIS MODEL — see FREE_AI_PROVIDERS.md for the comparison.
# In short: free with no card, does not retain inference data by default, Zero
# Data Retention is free for every account, and llama-3.3-70b-versatile is a
# production NON-reasoning model. That last part matters here: a reasoning
# model spends max_tokens on thinking first and can return an empty answer, the
# failure script_engine.py already documents from TokenRouter.
#
# DEVELOPMENT ONLY until the privacy policy names Groq. script_engine prints
# that warning on start, and it is right: a writer's draft goes to whoever is
# named here, and Privacy_Policy.md currently names Anthropic.
#
# Login: test@example.com / password
BAAKHAPAA_DEMO=1
LLM_PROVIDER=groq
GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile
# Keep every PAID provider off. OpenAI drives storyboard images (DALL-E), which
# stay as placeholders here.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
PAYMENT_SANDBOX=false
